## 6. Add the runner to the approved PR workflow

The supplied script runs `danger ci`, appends a report, and emails it. Its credential and logging operations require changes before use. Section 8 contains a redacted review copy.

The following is an **adaptation for review**, using the locked local CLI, explicit rules path, report overwrite, and a preserved exit status. It also adds `--failOnErrors` so a rule failure can fail the step. Confirm the option and paths with the approved installed Danger version. [Danger failure behavior](https://danger.systems/js/guides/getting_started.html)

**File — `scripts/ci/run-danger.sh`.** This runs on the trusted Bitrise PR runner after checkout and dependency installation.

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
set +x
umask 077

: "${WORKDIR:?Set WORKDIR to the application package root}"
: "${DANGER_GITHUB_API_TOKEN:?Protected Danger token is required}"
: "${DANGER_GITHUB_HOST:?GitHub Enterprise host is required}"
: "${DANGER_GITHUB_API_BASE_URL:?GitHub Enterprise API URL is required}"

cd "$WORKDIR"
test -f src/danger/dangerfile.ts
test -x node_modules/.bin/danger

DANGER_EXIT_CODE=0
if ./node_modules/.bin/danger ci \
  --dangerfile src/danger/dangerfile.ts \
  --failOnErrors > src/danger/DangerReport.log 2>&1; then
  DANGER_EXIT_CODE=0
else
  DANGER_EXIT_CODE=$?
fi

printf 'Danger finished with exit code %s. Inspect the PR and protected report.\n' "$DANGER_EXIT_CODE"
exit "$DANGER_EXIT_CODE"
```

**Integration excerpt —** merge this Script step into the approved trusted PR workflow after dependency installation. It is a new wrapper around the runner above, rather than a verbatim source YAML block.

