### Request file and upload ownership

The pinned private app-create example reads `.sauce/saucelabs_request.yml`. The latest reference names that file but omits its complete schema. Obtain the schema from the step owner before creating the file. Earlier material uses different request paths and contracts.

The reference also supplies a standalone upload script and a `saucectl` execution script. Use one approved upload strategy, and confirm how registration, application storage ID, and test-runner storage ID connect before combining commands. The full guide lives in [Testing & Quality](../testing-quality/sauce-labs-real-device-testing.mdx).

```bash
RESPONSE=$(curl -u "$SAUCE_USERNAME:$SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY" \
  --location \
  --request POST 'https://api.us-west-1.saucelabs.com/v1/storage/upload' \
  -F "payload=@$APP_PATH" \
  -F "name=$(basename "$APP_PATH")")

APP_ID=$(echo "$RESPONSE" | jq -r '.item.id')
envman add --key SAUCE_APP_ID --value "$APP_ID"
echo "Uploaded app to Sauce Labs. Storage ID: $APP_ID"
```

